# Working Agreements

## Keep docs in sync with the conversation

Treat `docs/` as living documentation. After any conversation that changes scope,
decisions, architecture, API shape, or UX, update the relevant doc in the same turn:

| Change is about… | Update… |
|------------------|---------|
| Scope, goals, decisions, phases | `docs/spec.md` |
| Components, stack, data flow, schema | `docs/architecture.md` |
| Endpoints, payloads, contracts | `docs/api.md` |
| UX, interactions, flows | `docs/design.md` |
| Process, principles, skill workflow | `docs/development.md` |

- Update docs **automatically in the same turn** as the decision — do not wait to be asked.
- Keep `docs/README.md` index accurate when docs are added or removed.
- Reflect what was actually built, not just what was planned (e.g. note tech swaps).
- Prefer concise, structured edits over prose dumps. No "TBD" / placeholder slop.

## Always ask for clarification

When scope, intent, or a tradeoff is ambiguous, ask before acting. Prefer a short
multiple-choice question over guessing. Confirm destructive or scope-expanding actions.

## Use skills for planning, scope, and project management

For anything involving planning, scope changes, reframing, task breakdown, or
estimating work, read and follow
`.agents/skills/planning-and-task-breakdown/SKILL.md` before proceeding.

**Switch to Plan mode** for this work: plan read-only, produce ordered, verifiable
tasks, and get explicit approval before writing any code.

Every build plan must include **two diagrams**: data flow (code/state) and user
experience (interaction sequence — what changes for the person using the tool).

See `docs/development.md` Phase workflow.

## Available project skills

Check these before doing related work and follow the relevant one:

| Skill | Use for |
|-------|---------|
| `planning-and-task-breakdown` | Planning, scope, task breakdown, project management |
| `pi-planning-with-files` | Larger multi-feature planning across files |
| `find-skills` | Discovering/installing new skills when a capability is missing |
| `frontend-design` | Building or restyling UI |
| `web-design-guidelines` | UI/UX quality and design review |
| `vercel-react-best-practices` | Writing/reviewing React code |
| `vercel-composition-patterns` | React component architecture/composition |
| `webapp-testing` | Testing the web app |
| `agent-browser` | Driving a browser to verify behavior |

When a task matches a skill, read its `SKILL.md` and follow it rather than working from memory.
